    {
      "id": "dbec6ef0-b7fd-4dce-9a26-b707629f5d88",
      "name": "Intake and HMAC explanation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -944,
        -32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 672,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## 1. Receive and sign the payload\n\nThis intake group receives the AppsMax webhook as raw bytes and calculates HMAC-SHA256 with the secret stored in the Crypto credential."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1f802b81-073f-474a-81b1-ae3266c6e87a",
      "name": "Validation and filtering explanation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -224,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 672,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "## 2. Validate and filter events\n\nThis group compares the calculated and received signatures, rejects invalid requests, and forwards only `application.created`. Other valid event types are acknowledged without calling the destination."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6d715ec8-aeb2-4ce5-8d33-8fde81caddd9",
      "name": "Mapping and delivery explanation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        480,
        -224
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 336,
        "content": "## 3. Map and forward the lead\n\nThis group selects the minimum lead fields, builds a stable idempotency key, and posts the JSON payload to the HTTPS endpoint you control."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4e1b4bfd-a6d7-4b64-bdc1-e25a88103341",
      "name": "Delivery result explanation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        944,
        -272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 496,
        "content": "## 4. Handle the delivery result\n\nThis group returns success only for downstream `2xx`. A downstream `4xx`, `5xx`, timeout, or network failure becomes `502` so AppsMax can apply its delivery retry policy."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9e594cc7-54ed-4768-aefb-8fa847a453fc",
      "name": "Workflow overview and setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -900,
        -1480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 1400,
        "height": 980,
        "content": "## Forward verified AppsMax lead webhooks to an external HTTPS API\n\n### Who this is for\nUse this workflow when AppsMax already receives website applications and you need to continue processing each new lead in a CRM, ERP, help desk, data pipeline, or another HTTPS API through n8n. It uses only standard n8n nodes and is not a native AppsMax node.\n\n### How it works\nThe Webhook node receives an AppsMax `application.created` event with its raw request body. Crypto calculates HMAC-SHA256 with the shared webhook secret, and Code compares the calculated and received lowercase-hex signatures. Invalid requests return `401`. Other event types, including `application.test`, return `204` without calling the destination. Valid new applications are reduced to the minimum lead fields and sent to your API with an `Idempotency-Key`. AppsMax receives `200` only after the destination returns `2xx`; downstream errors return `502` so the AppsMax delivery policy can retry.\n\n### Requirements\n- An AppsMax project with an outgoing application webhook enabled\n- n8n with the standard Webhook, Crypto, Code, If, Edit Fields, HTTP Request, and Respond to Webhook nodes\n- A controlled HTTPS endpoint that accepts JSON and deduplicates requests\n\n### Setup\nFollow the safety checklist below. Keep secrets in n8n credentials, replace both placeholders, run the test matrix, and activate the workflow only after the checks pass. See the [AppsMax n8n guide](https://appsmax.ru/kb/kak-podklyuchit-appsmax-k-n8n/) for the AppsMax-side steps.\n\n### Customize\nChange the Edit Fields mapping to match your destination schema. Add destination authentication through an n8n credential. Preserve the signature check, idempotency header, and explicit `2xx` gate when adding branches. Test with synthetic data before production."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d61eb471-dc7c-4614-9994-ddbc2f143d27",
      "name": "Production safety gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -900,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 330,
        "content": "## Setup before activation\n\n1. Replace the webhook path with a long random value.\n2. Create a Crypto credential and put the AppsMax webhook secret in **HMAC Secret**. Attach it only to **HMAC raw body**.\n3. Replace `example.invalid` with the controlled HTTPS API endpoint and configure its authentication as an n8n credential.\n4. The downstream endpoint must treat `Idempotency-Key` as idempotent and return `2xx` for both the first accepted call and an already accepted duplicate.\n5. Keep the explicit `2xx` gate: downstream `4xx`, `5xx`, timeout or network failure must return `502` to AppsMax so its delivery policy can retry.\n6. Test valid signature, invalid signature, `application.test`, one created event, one downstream failure and a replay before publishing the workflow.\n\nDo not paste secrets into nodes, URLs, notes or exported JSON."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
